            "description": "<p>The consumer is <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/consumer-spending-holds-strong-heres-183000373.html\">still spending</a> but is <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/retail-sales-show-us-consumer-spending-holds-up-but-almost-everyone-is-looking-for-deals-171632523.html\">prioritizing value</a> due to <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/why-consumer-confidence-just-hit-150850134.html\">shaken confidence</a>.</p>\n<p>Loop Capital Markets managing director Anthony Chukumba joins Market Domination to discuss what the state of the consumer means for investors and how to play discount retailer names like Dollar Tree (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DLTR\">DLTR</a>), Five Below (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/FIVE\">FIVE</a>), and Ollie's (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/OLLI\">OLLI</a>).</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination/\">Market Domination</a>.</p>",
